BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.visitnapavalley.com/event/press-%7c-learn-to-make-ricotta-gnudi/18076/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:PRESS | Learn to Make Ricotta Gnudi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T000000
UID:261113UGvHH_EctE2i4KFo7cRDQg
DESCRIPTION:A Hands-On Class in the Art of Handmade Pasta Step into the Un
 der-Study Teaching Kitchen to learn the art of handmade pasta and craft on
 e of PRESS' most beloved signature dishes: delicate ricotta gnudi. Guests 
 will be welcomed with a glass of champagne before being guided through eve
 ry step of the process\, from mixing and shaping the perfect pillows of ri
 cotta to plating them with seasonal accompaniments that highlight their el
 egant simplicity. Along the way\, you'll gain professional tips on working
  with fresh cheese\, hear stories from the PRESS kitchen\, and discover wh
 at makes gnudi a timeless staple on our menu. After class\, settle in for 
 a three-course lunch featuring the ricotta gnudi you've prepared\, complem
 ented by seasonal dishes inspired by the menus of PRESS and Under-Study. W
 hether you're a curious home cook or an experienced foodie\, this is a rar
 e opportunity to step inside the kitchen\, learn professional techniques\,
  and enjoy a memorable meal centered around one of PRESS' most iconic dish
 es. In this class\, you will learn: • How to make light\, delicate ricot
 ta gnudi from scratch • Professional tips for working with fresh cheese 
 and pasta dough • The fundamentals of restaurant-quality plating and pre
 sentation • How seasonal ingredients and accompaniments enhance the fini
 shed dish • Insights and stories from the PRESS kitchen behind one of ou
 r signature menu items Only attendees who are 21\\+ may take part in alcoh
 olic beverages.
URL:https://www.visitnapavalley.com/event/press-%7c-learn-to-make-ricotta-
 gnudi/18076/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/the-santa-rosa-original-certified-farmers-market/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T000000
UID:260606i9_7yrNARkiA-16fNKqiCw
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market is a year-rou
 nd Saturday tradition in Sonoma County\, bringing together local farmers\,
  ranchers\, food artisans\, and neighbors from 8:30 a.m. to 1 p.m. This is
  not just a place to shop\, it's a place to connect directly with the peop
 le who grow your food. As a Slow Food Sonoma County award recipient\, the 
 market prioritizes integrity\, seasonality\, and true farm-to-community re
 lationships. Expect peak-season produce harvested just hours before market
 \, pasture-raised meats\, fresh flowers\, artisan breads\, handcrafted goo
 ds\, and thoughtfully prepared foods that reflect the region's agricultura
 l richness. Visitors can stroll the vibrant open-air market\, sample local
  flavors\, and experience Sonoma County's food culture in its most authent
 ic form. Families\, chefs\, and weekend explorers alike gather here to dis
 cover what's growing now and to support small farms that keep our local fo
 od system strong. Open every Saturday\, rain or shine\, the Santa Rosa Ori
 ginal Certified Farmers Market is a cornerstone of the community and a mus
 t-visit stop for anyone wanting to taste\, shop\, and experience Sonoma Co
 unty at its freshest.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
