SUMMARY:The (Unbelievably True) Story of Nicky O
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T153000
UID:261113Ao2uwB-nMkaNVsEmLUiOGg
DESCRIPTION:The \\(Unbelievably True\\) Story of Nicky O\, a new rock musi
 cal based on an incredible true story. Nicky O’Neill was an aspiring tee
 nage rockstar when\, in 2003\, he became the youngest victim in the deadly
  Station Nightclub fire. Following his death\, a series of surprising supe
 rnatural events unfolded\, uniting his family & friends in the belief that
  Nicky is forever watching over them from above.\n\nWith original music by
  Nicky O’Neill and friends\, alongside a brand new book by local thespia
 n \\(and Nicky’s sister-in-law\\) Maureen O’Neill\, Nicky O is a movin
 g\, heartfelt\, and surprisingly funny message that our loved ones are nev
 er gone…they walk among us.
LOCATION:Rancho Cotate High School
URL:https://omella.com/o04kd
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-from-away-tickets-2003472917428", "Press Democrat": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-from-away-tickets-2003472917428"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-from-away-tickets-2003472917428"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Come From Away: Marin's First Production of the Tony-Winning Music
 al
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T150000
UID:261108-LQeTQlQg0u-HxQCe_U01Q
DESCRIPTION:A Tony-winning Broadway hit is coming to San Anselmo\, and it'
 s the first time it's ever been performed in Marin.\n\n**Come From Away**\
 n\nBook\, Music and Lyrics by Irene Sankoff and David Hein\n\nOn 9/11\, 38
  planes were suddenly grounded in a tiny town in Newfoundland. Overnight\,
  the locals took in nearly 7\,000 stranded travelers from around the world
 \, and strangers became family. This is their true story\, and it's funny\
 , uplifting and full of heart\, with a live band of musicians from Marin's
  Irish music scene.\n\nSan Domenico School's production marks the 25th ann
 iversary of 9/11.\n\nShow times:\n\n**Friday\, November 13 at 7pm**\n\n**S
 aturday\, November 14 at 1pm and 7pm**\n\n**Sunday\, November 15 at 3pm**\
 n\nTickets: $15 general\, $10 students and seniors\n\nRun time: About 2 ho
 urs\, including intermission\n\nFree parking. Wheelchair accessible.\n\n**
 Saturday night still has the best seats!**\n\n*Please be advised that adul
 t language and the mention of difficult subject matter\, including Islamop
 hobia and 9/11\, are included in this show.*\n\nCome From Away is presente
 d through special arrangement with Music Theatre International (MTI). MTI 
 also supplies all authorized performance materials. www.MTIShows.com
LOCATION:Carol Franc Buck Hall of the Arts\, San Domenico School
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-f
 rom-away-tickets-2003472917428
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
