BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://vfwpost1943.org", "Press Democrat": "http://vfwpost1943.org"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://vfwpost1943.org"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Veterans Holiday Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:260930cqiS-yivFUq6ErM_n0Pnsw
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma VFW Auxiliary Post 1943 will host its 4th Annual Ve
 terans Holiday Market on Saturday\, November 14\, from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\,
  and Sunday\, November 15\, from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m. at the Veterans Memoria
 l Building\, 126 First St. West\, Sonoma.\n\nThe two-day holiday market wi
 ll feature one-of-a-kind\, limited-edition goods handcrafted by local arti
 sts and makers. With several vendors participating\, shoppers will have an
  opportunity to find unique gifts while supporting the Auxiliary’s missi
 on of helping those who have served and their loved ones.\n\nThe Native Da
 ughters of the Golden West\, Sonoma Parlor No. 209\, will also host a spec
 ial community activity\, “Make a Veteran a Christmas Card.” Community 
 members of all ages are invited to create handmade holiday cards that will
  be delivered to area veterans living in assisted living facilities and nu
 rsing homes.\n\nThe Veterans Holiday Market is free and open to the public
 \, with a special invitation extended to military members\, veterans and t
 heir families. Proceeds from the event will help provide assistance to vet
 erans and military families who are experiencing hardship.\n\nThe VFW Auxi
 liary is an all-volunteer service organization whose members include the s
 pouses\, parents\, grandparents\, brothers\, sisters and other family memb
 ers of those who have served in overseas combat. Since 1934\, members of S
 onoma VFW Auxiliary Post 1943 have worked to support those who have served
  and strengthen the community around them.\n\nThe Auxiliary’s community 
 service efforts have included toy and monetary donations to Toys for Tots\
 , Christmas gifts and cards for veterans at the Yountville Veterans Home\,
  as well as clothing and food drives benefiting local emergency service or
 ganizations.\n\nThe Veterans Holiday Market is an opportunity for the enti
 re community to come together during the holiday season—not only to shop
  and celebrate\, but also to show appreciation for those who have served a
 nd to remind veterans and their loved ones that they are valued\, remember
 ed and not alone.\n\nVeteran Families Helping Veterans\n\nFor more informa
 tion contact: Debbie Chandler \\(707\\)364-2734
LOCATION:Sonoma Veterans Building
URL:http://vfwpost1943.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
