X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-from-away-tickets-2003472917428", "Press Democrat": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-from-away-tickets-2003472917428"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-from-away-tickets-2003472917428"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Come From Away: Marin's First Production of the Tony-Winning Music
 al
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:2611080s6CzmDqakiGIXV0tYkOKQ
DESCRIPTION:A Tony-winning Broadway hit is coming to San Anselmo\, and it'
 s the first time it's ever been performed in Marin.\n\n**Come From Away**\
 n\nBook\, Music and Lyrics by Irene Sankoff and David Hein\n\nOn 9/11\, 38
  planes were suddenly grounded in a tiny town in Newfoundland. Overnight\,
  the locals took in nearly 7\,000 stranded travelers from around the world
 \, and strangers became family. This is their true story\, and it's funny\
 , uplifting and full of heart\, with a live band of musicians from Marin's
  Irish music scene.\n\nSan Domenico School's production marks the 25th ann
 iversary of 9/11.\n\nShow times:\n\n**Friday\, November 13 at 7pm**\n\n**S
 aturday\, November 14 at 1pm and 7pm**\n\n**Sunday\, November 15 at 3pm**\
 n\nTickets: $15 general\, $10 students and seniors\n\nRun time: About 2 ho
 urs\, including intermission\n\nFree parking. Wheelchair accessible.\n\n**
 Saturday night still has the best seats!**\n\n*Please be advised that adul
 t language and the mention of difficult subject matter\, including Islamop
 hobia and 9/11\, are included in this show.*\n\nCome From Away is presente
 d through special arrangement with Music Theatre International (MTI). MTI 
 also supplies all authorized performance materials. www.MTIShows.com
LOCATION:Carol Franc Buck Hall of the Arts\, San Domenico School
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/san-domenico-upper-school-presents-come-f
 rom-away-tickets-2003472917428
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040036054?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Misner & Smith Matinee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:261031bVUi234JjUSUChsP-7EO-Q
DESCRIPTION:Misner & Smith's music is a rare combination of poetic\, story
 -filled songwriting lifted to exquisite heights by masterful vocal harmoni
 es.\n\nFollowing the release of their critically acclaimed new album\, All
  is Song\, Northern California-based unclassifiable duo Misner & Smith ret
 urn to HopMonk Sebastopol - The Abbey - for another evening of masterful v
 ocal harmonies and extraordinary songwriting. With All is Song they turn i
 n their finest work to date--an album of inspired declarations to the powe
 r of music\, song\, and collaboration. Their live shows are no different\,
  and the beauty of their vocal harmonies combined with truly inventive son
 gwriting has made the band one of the most inspiring acts in the Americana
  world. Blending elements of that genre with rock\, traditional folk\, and
  more pop-leaning ideas\, Misner & Smith makes music gloriously nonconform
 ing.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040036054?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108940639?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Jim Lauderdale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:261020kBWWUaoHz0W9mh3CxXJ0pw
DESCRIPTION:Two-time Grammy-winning singer and master songwriter Jim Laude
 rdale is both a "songwriter's songwriter\," who's written/co-written many 
 modern classics for iconic artists\, as well as an intuitive sideman\, who
 's enhanced the music of a bevy of esteemed musicians. As a solo artist\, 
 since 1986 up until now\, he's created a bodywork spanning 37 albums of im
 aginative roots music\, encompassing all that is today’s musical landsca
 pe. His combination of Country\, Bluegrass\, Soul\, R&B and Rock has helpe
 d to pave the way for the current Americana movement.\n\nFor several decad
 es\, Jim has written songs for and worked with some of the finest artists 
 in traditional and modern music including Ralph Stanley\, Elvis Costello\,
  George Strait\, Buddy Miller\, Lucinda Williams\, John Oates\, Solomon Bu
 rke\, Lee Ann Womack\, Old Crow Medicine Show\, Mary Chapin Carpenter\, Bl
 ake Shelton\, the Dixie Chicks\, Vince Gill\, Patty Loveless\, and Gary Al
 lan among others.\n\nLauderdale co-hosts "The Buddy & Jim Show" weekly rad
 io program on SiriusXM with Buddy Miller. Recently\, the Americana Music A
 ssociation honoured him with the WagonMaster Lifetime Achievement Award. J
 im has certainly earned it\, having released a staggering 37 albums with t
 he latest My Favorite Place out June 21st on Sky Crunch Records 2024. \n\n
 Whether solo or band\, Jim Lauderdale a triple threat performer\, songwrit
 er and musician who is constantly reinventing himself!
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108940639?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
