SUMMARY:Bottega Cellar Series with Stag's Leap Wine Cellars
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T210000
UID:261006NtPiSXxMakmHqr0VDmhRQg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Bottega on November 17 for an elegant evening featu
 ring Stag’s Leap Wine Cellars\, hosted by Winemaker Marcus Notaro. Stag'
 s Leap Wine Cellars is a legendary Napa Valley estate established by Warre
 n Winiarski in 1970 in the Stags Leap District. Just six years after its f
 ounding\, its 1973 S.L.V. Cabernet Sauvignon stunned the world by besting 
 top Bordeaux wines\, including two First-Growths\, at the 1976 Judgment of
  Paris\, a victory that put California and Napa Valley on the global winem
 aking map. Join longtime winemaker Marcus Notaro as the estate continues i
 ts year-long 50th anniversary celebration of the Judgment of Paris. Guests
  will experience a thoughtfully curated progression of wines showcasing th
 e depth and character of the estate\, from vibrant whites to distinguished
  Napa Valley Cabernet Sauvignon\, paired with a seasonal multi-course menu
  by Bottega Executive Chef Alex Espinoza. Each course is designed to compl
 ement the character and expression of the wines\, bringing together refine
 d flavors\, exceptional ingredients\, and the gracious hospitality that de
 fines Bottega.\n\nPrice is inclusive of tax and gratuity.\n\n6525 Washingt
 on Street Suite A9\, Yountville\, CA 94599\n\n(707) 945-1050
LOCATION:Bottega Napa Valley
URL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=25489&r
 estref=25489&experienceId=791062&utm_source=external&utm_medium=referral&u
 tm_campaign=shared
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.jewishpetaluma.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7522546/jewish/The-Kabbalah-of-Meaning.htm", "Press Democrat": "https://www.jewishpetaluma.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7522546/jewish/The-Kabbalah-of-Meaning.htm"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.jewishpetaluma.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7522546/jewish/The-Kabbalah-of-Meaning.htm"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Kabbalah of Meaning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T193000
UID:261001_fTlK71MKk2JU-SZOeSjcg
DESCRIPTION:Jewish Wisdom for a Life That Matters\n\nNo matter how much we
  achieve\, something within us still asks: “Is this it? Isn’t there so
 mething more?”\n\nThe Kabbalah of Meaning is a new six-session JLI cours
 e exploring the Jewish answer to that question. What are we really searchi
 ng for—and where can it be found?\n\nDrawing on Kabbalah and centuries o
 f Jewish wisdom\, we’ll uncover the essential building blocks of a deepl
 y meaningful life. We’ll explore how purpose can be found in our work\, 
 relationships\, challenges\, accomplishments\, and even the ordinary routi
 nes that fill our days.\n\nYou don’t have to revamp your life. You don
 ’t need to meditate on a mountaintop. You simply need a new lens through
  which to see the rich world of meaning already woven into every part of y
 our life.\n\nThoughtful\, practical\, and surprisingly relevant\, this cou
 rse offers fresh perspectives and useful tools for living with greater cla
 rity\, connection\, and intention.\n\nTry 1st class free.\n\nNo previous J
 ewish learning required. Come as you are—and bring your questions.
LOCATION:Chabad Jewish Center of Petaluma
URL:https://www.jewishpetaluma.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7522546/je
 wish/The-Kabbalah-of-Meaning.htm
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
