SUMMARY:WRECKLESS STRANGERS
DESCRIPTION:DINNER SHOW with WRECKLESS STRANGERS\nWreckless Strangers is a collective of friends and musicians carrying the torch for San Francisco’s grand rock ‘n’ roll tradition. Their unique blend of “Ameri-Cali Soul” melds the contemporary blues stylings of Bonnie Raitt and Boz Scaggs; the songwriting sensibilities of Sons of Champlin and Fleetwood Mac; the swashbuckling Americana of the Lost Planet Airmen and Peter Rowan; and the funk of Sly Stone and Tower of Power with a dash of Grateful Dead and Jefferson Airplane for flavor and unpredictability. With soaring vocal harmonies and burning instrumental improvisation framed in concise and poignant original songwriting\, Wreckless Strangers seek to honor and carry forth the brand of free-spirited musical fun and adventure that defines the Bay Area. \n 
URL:https://ranchonicasio.com/event/wreckless-strangers-4/
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio\, 1 Old Rancheria Rd\, Nicasio\, CA\, 94946\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ranchonicasio.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Wreckless_Strangers_PressPhoto2026-002-resized-2026.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/prescription-for-poetry"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Prescription for Poetry  — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Cali
 fornia
DTSTART:20261120T000000
DTEND:20261121T000000
UID:9252883fa1b1d01a7cf3d8613631a5bf@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Prescription for Poetry - November 20th\, 2026\n\n  \n    \n  
     \n        \n          $45.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nFriday\, N
 ovember 20th\, 2026 1:00-5:00pm Fee for this session: $45.00 Prescription 
 for Poetry: A Deeper Dive into Poetic Medicine in Community As a Source of
  HealingSince March 2025\, Redwing Keyssar has been leading monthly Poetic
  Medicine sessions at Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, gathering a vibrant
  community of folks who listen to an write poems together\, as a deeply me
 aningful source of healing\, inspiration and connection. Many people retur
 n each month\, and new folks come and go as well. There has been a yearnin
 g for more time to do this work together in community\, to have time and s
 pace to delve deeper into the thoughts and feelings that emerge and surpri
 se us\, as we hold silence together\, as well as listen deeply and write e
 ffortlessly. And so… we are now offering a seasonal 4-hour Poetic Medici
 ne Session\, beginning on Friday\, November 20th\, from 1:00-5:00pm!What t
 o Bring: your pen/paper/journal/laptop your water bottle your open heart\,
  be ready to be surprised! Some light snacks will be provided. As with the
  monthly sessions: The practice of “poem making” offers a means to exp
 ress the metaphors and meaning of the joys and suffering we experience in 
 ourselves and bear witness to in others. Poetry can be a salve for the hea
 rt and soul. It is a way of speaking what is try in our hearts and is ofte
 n difficult to access without a creative spark. You do not have to be a 
 “poet” or even a “writer” to allow words and feelings to pour thro
 ugh your heart and your pen. Come find the magic in yourself and in the co
 mmunity. About the Instructor: Redwing Keyssar has been leading “Poetic 
 Medicine in Community” sessions through her work in Palliative Care at U
 CSF since 2020. Her work has created an international community of people 
 who\, by listening to and writing poetry together\, have healed wounds of 
 grief and loss\, helped ”wounded healers\,” and provided resiliency to
  move forward on our life paths.Redwing is a Palliative Care nurse\, educa
 tor and consultant\, an end-of-life doula\, author\, poet\, song-writer\, 
 ceremonialist\, national presenter and frequent contributor to public issu
 es about Palliative and End of Life Care. She is a Board member of the Seb
 astopol Senior Center and offers presentations about end-of-life issues th
 roughout the Bay Area. Before working at the UCSF MERI CENTER\, her profes
 sional career included being the Clinical Director at Zen Hospice Project 
 and the Director of Palliative Care and Nursing at Jewish Family and Child
 ren’s Services from 2004-2018. She is a founder and adjunct faculty memb
 er of the California State University Shiley/Haynes Institute of Palliativ
 e Care and has taught courses at OLLI at Sonoma State. Redwing is the auth
 or of an award-winning book\, “Last Acts of Kindness\; Lessons for the L
 iving from the Bedsides of the Dying” and is the recipient of numerous a
 wards in the field of Palliative Care.She is passionate about utilizing po
 etry as a healing modality!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n             
    Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/prescription-for-poetry
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
