X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/paint-your-pets-portrait-watercolor-for-all-levels/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Paint Your Pet's Portrait: Watercolor for All Levels
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T130000
UID:261031NUhfyd5lVkqLvSGJLqv-VQ
DESCRIPTION:Fridays Weekly · 3 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nNovember 6 – Nov
 ember 20\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategor
 y\n\nDrawing & Painting\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Leve
 ls\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$225\n\nMaterials Fee:
 \n\n$10\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$235\n\nChoose a favorite photo of 
 a pet and learn how to render it as a watercolor portrait. Over three week
 s\, you’ll receive instruction from an artist who has painted many commi
 ssioned pet portraits in watercolor. Instructor Hannah Day will share her 
 insights and her approach to rendering animals in this medium\, guiding yo
 u through a layering process that builds vibrancy\, detail\, and depth.Whe
 ther you’re new to watercolor or have experience with the medium\, this 
 class offers an engaging way to develop your skills while creating a perso
 nal portrait of a beloved pet. Your finished painting can be a meaningful 
 keepsake—or a unique holiday gift.You’re welcome to email your photo t
 o us ahead of class\, and we’ll print it for you to use as a reference.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/paint-your-pets-portrait-wa
 tercolor-for-all-levels/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T170000
UID:261004gbcCjIiXfUGgt9btixyhfw
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
