SUMMARY:Holiday Boutique
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T140000
UID:261113_mTlzJSVNkyV7bkPiYVFhg
DESCRIPTION:St. Paul's Holiday Boutique is almost here! The sparkling even
 t that takes place annually the Saturday before Thanksgiving begins at 10 
 a.m. Saturday\, Nov. 21 at the St. Paul's Episcopal Church parish hall\, 2
 09 Matheson St. in Healdsburg. We offer items to streamline your holiday p
 reparation and gift-giving\, and who can't use a helping hand during this 
 jam-packed season. Look for our wide assortment of jams\, jellies\, marmal
 ade\, preserves\, chutneys and candies\; and baked goods of all kinds incl
 uding cookies\, pies and breads that can be served now or frozen for later
 . Pick up jars of bean-soup mix to simmer and serve a crowd\; and a favori
 te for gifting: cookie mixes that are prettily packaged\; just add your ow
 n egg and butter\, stir up and bake for a one-bowl batch of homemade cooki
 es in a flash. And there are plenty of other items to make your holidays b
 righter: We offer a wide selection of lovely costume jewelry along with ho
 liday decorations\, housewares\, serving pieces\, linens and toys. Stop by
  and see! Nearby parking is free.
LOCATION:St. Paul's Episcopal Church parish hall
URL:http://www.stpauls-healdsburg.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/stone-wrapping"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Stone Wrapping Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T150000
UID:261106pX_D7msS20-X_SbajIZq1Q
DESCRIPTION:In this class\, students will be creating decorative stones\, 
 utilizing wrapping techniques that can be applied outside of this class. S
 tudents will learn 3 basic knots with time allotted between each lesson fo
 r students to experiment creating new stones with the new knot. This appro
 ach allows everyone’s imagination to run wild\, fostering creativity and
  allowing time for new ideas.\n\nAll materials provided.\n\nStudents often
  make 6-8 stones per class.\n\nThere will be discussion breaks\, and a lun
 ch break throughout the class. Please bring water and a paper bag lunch.\n
 \nAbout the Teacher: Carrie Botto is a self taught multi-medium weaver. Sh
 e started weaving with beads over 40 years ago and continues to add skills
  and techniques to her “tool box”. Carrie travels all over the country
  now teaching several different classes\, and has taught at Mendocino Art 
 Center\, New Mexico Bead Trader\, Moab Art Center\, and Fiber on 4th in Ne
 w Mexico. Follow Carrie on Instagram @beanstreetsudio!
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/stone-wrapping
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
