BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.reusealliance.org/events/petaluma-repairfair", "Press Democrat": "https://www.reusealliance.org/events/petaluma-repairfair"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.reusealliance.org/events/petaluma-repairfair"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Petaluma Repair Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T130000
UID:261021QtXAW-RnBEK1bByA9jhLsA
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a lamp\, small appliance\, textile\, or bike in ne
 ed of repair?\n\n**Bring it to the Repair Fair!**‍ ‍\n\nVolunteers and
  specialized repair professionals will be on-hand to repair**\\*** your it
 ems.  We ask that you stay with your item while it's being fixed\, so yo
 u can learn tips for future maintenance\, how to shop for repairable goods
 \, and even how to repair things yourself!  \n\n**If you’d like to b
 ring an item to repair\, please register the item here:** https://www.reus
 ealliance.org/rf-reg (Pre-registering allows us to prepare for your item!)
 \n\nThis is a free public event.\n\nThis event will also include a **Holid
 ay Swap & Clothing Swap!** Bring holiday decor\, clothing and accessories 
 to share and take home something new-to-you. Please limit donations to 1 b
 ag per person (clean and good condition only\, no undergarments or socks p
 lease)\, but take as much as you’d like! More about clothing swaps here.
 \n\n***\\*We cannot guarantee your item(s) will be repaired\, depending on
  the existing damage or breakage\, ability of volunteer fixers\, and avail
 ability of materials for repair. Note: we cannot work on microwaves\, repa
 ir screens on cell phones/computer devices\, or perform any welding/brazi
 ng\, but we are happy to refer you to professionals who can. In addition\,
  the textile department is not able to perform the following:***\n\n***Rep
 lacing zippers***\n\n***Repairing shoes\, leather\, or vinyl materials***\
 n\n***Performing alterations (making garments bigger/smaller)***\n\n***Rep
 lacing rivets/grommets***\n\n***Hemming certain fabrics (stretchy fabric\,
  sleek/luxury fabrics e.g. prom dresses)***\n\n***If you are in need of ga
 rment hemming\, we require that you please pin your garment to the desired
  length before you arrive.***\n\n**Join Us!**\n\nDo you enjoy fixing thing
 s?  Or want to help out in other ways?  We need you! **Sign up or email
  volunteer@reusealliance.org if you have any questions.**
LOCATION:Petaluma Community Center
URL:https://www.reusealliance.org/events/petaluma-repairfair
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/lionstigersbears2026", "Press Democrat": "https://sec.regfox.com/lionstigersbears2026"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/lionstigersbears2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Animals of Sugarloaf
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T143000
UID:261007pj14SbV_M02D-q2FC_OLtg
DESCRIPTION:November can be a very peaceful time at Sugarloaf. We
 t or dry\, it’s the month for nature to take a moment. But 
 the animals are still here. Birds call\, Coyotes yip and if you
  turn over the wrong rock you may hear a rattle. However\, for
  most\, their presence requires a bit of sleuthing. A broken tw
 ig lets us know a Mule tail deer was browsing\, some tootsie-ro
 ll like scat left by a Bobcat marks its territory\, a dirt and
  fir needle tower tells us there is a Turret Spider lurking be
 low. Join Certified California Naturalist John Lynch on a 4.1 mi
 le\, 4.5 hour hike from Lower Bald Mountain Trail over to the 
 Vista Trail down to and back on Meadow Trail. For this hike we
  need to sharpen our senses and put on our deerstalker caps. \
 n\nTickets are $10 for the general public\, $5 for students\, yo
 uth (12-17 year-olds)\, Sugarloaf members\, or Sugarloaf volunteers
 . Children between 7 and 12 can attend for free. Route not rec
 ommended for children under 7. All minors must be accompanied by
  a parent or legal guardian. Meet at the White Barn parking lo
 t. Bring at least a quart of water\, sun protection\, wear appr
 opriate clothing and footwear for slippery and rocky trails\, and
  if desired\, a snack. Parking fees apply. Heavy rains cancel.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/lionstigersbears2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.gvrd.org/wilson-park-community-outreach-meetings"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Wilson Park Community Outreach Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T113000
UID:261107EvR3qqV7ZkCt99nvvNi04A
DESCRIPTION:The City of Vallejo\, in partnership with the Greater Vallejo 
 Recreation District \\(GVRD\\)\, invites residents\, families\, and commun
 ity partners to help shape the future of Wilson Park!\n\nThe City is pursu
 ing funding through California's Statewide Park Development Grant Program 
 \\(Proposition 4\\) to support potential renovations and improvements to W
 ilson Park.\n\nThis is an exciting opportunity to explore ways to create a
  safer\, more welcoming\, accessible\, and vibrant neighborhood park for e
 veryone to enjoy.\n\nWhat Would You Like to See at Wilson Park? Your ideas
  can help identify potential park improvements\, including:\n\nNew recreat
 ional amenities and play features\n\nSafer\, more accessible spaces for al
 l ages and abilities\n\nLandscaping\, shade\, and beautification\n\nFamily
 -friendly gathering and relaxation areas\n\nOpportunities for recreation\,
  wellness\, and neighborhood connections\n\nNo final renovation plan has b
 een selected. Community input will help guide the proposed improvements.
LOCATION:GVRD Board Room
URL:https://www.gvrd.org/wilson-park-community-outreach-meetings
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T170000
UID:2610044WraOXTwikCNVBl901Wqjg
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T170000
UID:260824NsNO-yrTsEO6vuv2P2OdkA
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\nMaple Magic & Winter Wonder invites vis
 itors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativity\
 , and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided walks\,
  hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by the c
 hanging landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the swee
 t fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experience th
 e peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
