SUMMARY:The Mayflower: An Interesting Mix of Passengers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T143000
UID:2611089SQd2Kq9pEez4Wegu12lug
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society Presents\n\n The Mayflo
 wer: An Interesting Mix of Passengers\n\n Presented by Suzanne Brayer\n\n 
 In 1620\, an English merchant ship\, The Mayflower\, left Southampton Engl
 and for the New World carrying 102 men\, women\, children and a crew of 30
 . What motivated them to embark on this incredibly dangerous journey into 
 the unknown? In addition to the passengers\; the ship\, the journey\, The 
 Mayflower Compact\, the early history of the Plymouth Colony and the ubiqu
 itous myths\, these all make for fascinating stories.\n\n Ms. Brayer has 
 a BA from Indiana University and a MA in history and education from Arizon
 a State University. She enjoyed a career in secondary education for 30 yea
 rs. After retirement\, she became a professional genealogist. She is a pas
 t president of The Family History Society of Arizona\, a member of West Va
 lley Genealogy Society\, The Arizona Genealogy Advisory Board\, and numero
 us county societies in Indiana and North Carolina. She has taught genealog
 y classes and spoken to numerous groups throughout Arizona and the West.\n
 \n Saturday\, November 21st\n\n Meeting starts at 12:30 pm\, presentatio
 n starts at 1:00 pm PST\n\n Meeting Details : The meeting is held via Zoo
 m. Login begins at 12:30 p.m.\n\n FREE Via ZOOM\n\n Register at https:/
 /www.scgsonline.org\n\n Registration closes Friday\,  November 20th
URL:https://www.scgsonline.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
