SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T103000
UID:260728fObYJEjoiUiHIf802LF_Fg
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nIn OA\, membe
 rs experience spiritual\, emotional\, and physical recovery by practicing 
 the Twelve Steps and living by their spiritual principles—one day at a t
 ime.\n\nOvereaters Anonymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who suppor
 t each other in recovering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If y
 ou feel you have a problem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what yo
 ur background\, beliefs\, or eating habits. \n\nWe hold an in-person meet
 ings at 9:30 on Sunday mornings at Church of the Nazarene\, 18980 Arnold D
 rive\, Sonoma\, CA \\(a small room directly off of parking lot\; look for 
 the sign posted\\) and newcomers are always welcome.\n\nYou may view all N
 orth Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbayoa.org/me
 etings.html\n\nOA is not a diet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembe
 rs have different plans of eating.\n\nOA does not endorse any specific foo
 d plan. \n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meeting: https:/
 /www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
