X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://performingartsnapavalley.org/nvc-chorale-fall-26/", "Press Democrat": "https://performingartsnapavalley.org/nvc-chorale-fall-26/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://performingartsnapavalley.org/nvc-chorale-fall-26/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Napa Valley College Chorale - "A Hero's Journey"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T151500
UID:261013dOiLv_sCSUiCNgbvURxskg
DESCRIPTION:Every story worth telling begins the same way. Not with a plan
 . Not with a hero who is ready. \n\nIt begins with a call. \n\nJoseph Ca
 mpbell found the same journey running beneath human stories across every c
 ulture and every century: the ordinary life disrupted\, the threshold cros
 sed\, the road that takes everything\, the transformation that finally mak
 es the return possible. \n\n*A Hero’s Journey* is a choral concert bui
 lt on that arc. Five movements. One story. Music spanning Vivaldi to Rodge
 rs and Hammerstein\, a forgotten inscription on a cellar wall in wartime C
 ologne\, a Broadway meditation on hope written for a daughter\, ancient li
 turgy\, and a 21st-century voice asking\, quietly\, what it costs to get d
 ressed and show up. Between movements\, students from the NVC Reader’s T
 heater class give voice to the arc — narrating the journey from call to 
 return. \n\nThe NVC Chorale invites you to make the journey with them —
  a concert about the rest of us. The ones who weren’t ready. The ones 
 who went anyway.
LOCATION:Napa Valley College Performing Arts Center
URL:https://performingartsnapavalley.org/nvc-chorale-fall-26/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1599145155293030/1599145228626356/?active_tab=about"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Meet Me in St. Louis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T163000
UID:261112_AAP6cc9-0aoy95Nm9yHMA
DESCRIPTION:Meet Me in St. Louis is a heartwarming\, nostalgic musical tha
 t brings the charm and excitement of turn-of-the-century America to life. 
 Set in 1904 on the eve of the St. Louis World’s Fair\, the story follows
  the Smith family through a year of romance\, humor\, and unexpected chang
 e. At its center is the spirited and lovestruck Esther Smith\, whose bloss
 oming romance unfolds alongside her sisters’ own adventures and the fami
 ly’s hopes for the future. Featuring beloved songs like “The Trolley S
 ong\,” “Have Yourself a Merry Little Christmas\,” and “The Boy Nex
 t Door\,” this classic musical overflows with warmth\, wit\, and unforge
 ttable melodies. Rich with period detail\, lively ensemble numbers\, and t
 ender family moments\, Meet Me in St. Louis celebrates community\, resilie
 nce\, and the enduring power of home. Audiences will be swept up in its co
 lorful seasonal settings—from summer dances to a magical Christmas Eve
 —culminating in the dazzling anticipation of the World’s Fair. Perfect
  for theatregoers of all ages\, this timeless musical offers romance\, lau
 ghter\, and a joyful reminder that even in times of change\, love and fami
 ly light the way forward. MEET ME IN ST. LOUIS is presented by arrangement
  with Concord Theatricals on behalf of Tams-Witmark LLC. concordtheatrical
 s.com
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1599145155293030/1599145228626356/?act
 ive_tab=about
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
