BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://tinyurl.com/FlightLessonsNov22", "Press Democrat": "https://tinyurl.com/FlightLessonsNov22"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://tinyurl.com/FlightLessonsNov22"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Flight Lessons: A Folk Opera by Deborah Crooks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T164500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T190000
UID:261026tVBAN3Hmd0KDUF0C_ule4Q
DESCRIPTION:Based on a true story about Peregrine Falcons and humans livin
 g at the intersection of wild and urban habitats\, "Flight Lessons" is a t
 wo-act\, multi-character folk opera exploring themes of home\, adaptation 
 and recovery. The narrative-in-song follows an urban wildlife biologist wh
 o monitors the breeding pair of Peregrine Falcons nesting on a bridge and 
 how their lives intersect with the human inhabitants of the neighborhood a
 fter one of the birds is shot.  "Flight Lessons"  draws upon Deborah's e
 xperiences studying natural history and raptor conservation and features a
 n ensemble cast including Deborah\, Kwame Copeland\, Sean Lightholder\, Ka
 ren Mitchell\, Liz Stuart and Mick Shaffer.\n\n“FLIGHT LESSONS is a full
 \, rich story—the heroine’s journey—that takes us into the world of 
 urban birds.…remarkable and moving.”— Alameda Post\n\nhttps://debora
 hcrooks.com/flight-lessons
LOCATION:The Lost Church Santa Rosa
URL:https://tinyurl.com/FlightLessonsNov22
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
