X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/17699795"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Library Field Trip
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T170000
UID:261113NpwU2NcpZk6UVEPjCrPeEQ
DESCRIPTION:Pre-registration is required for this field trip due to limite
 d seats on transport. Transportation is provided. Please register each ind
 ividual participant in your party. Please arrive at the library by 8:30am 
 to check in. We will board the bus by 9am. The event will run from 10:30am
 -3:30pm\, not including transportation to and from the site. Please wear a
 ppropriate attire and comfortable shoes. Food will not be provided so plea
 se remember to pack your lunch\, snacks\, and water as needed. Participant
 s will need to sign a waiver provided on the day of the event. Brief Itine
 rary 8:30 am - Check in for Field Trip\, Collect Bus Waivers 9am - Board B
 uses\, depart from JFK 10 am - Arrive at Lake Solano\, Go over rules\, dis
 closures\, and activities with participants. Then split into 2 groups. 10:
 30am - 11:30am - Meet with Putah Creek\, Introductions Group A goes on Hik
 e Group B does activity provided 11:30am - 12:30pm - Switch Group A does a
 ctivity provided Group B goes on Hike 12:30pm - 1:30pm Break for Lunch Par
 ticipants provide their own food/drink Play/relax in nature picnic areas 1
 :30pm - 2:30pm - Explore the new native plant demonstration garden in uppe
 r day-use area 2:30pm - 3:00pm - Q & A w/ Putah Creek 3:00pm - 3:30pm - La
 st explorations/Down time to relax 3:30pm - Board buses\, depart from Lake
  Solano 4:45pm-5pm - Arrive back at JFK
