X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Livewhale": "https://santarosa.libcal.com/calendar/workshops/noodletools_mla_11_24_26"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research Cite It Right with NoodleTools @ 3pm
 \, Nov 24th
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261124T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261124T160000
DTSTAMP:20261113T152114Z
UID:20261124T230000Z-24413@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261124T150000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/644_cs_library_workshop_tour.rev.178605768
 7.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:Join SRJC Librarian Canon Crawford to learn how to simplify ci
 tations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the way\, score quick 
 tips on finding credible research in the library and on the Web.NoodleTool
 s helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliographies\, and offers no
 te-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\, including the capabil
 ity to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details: Extra Credit availab
 le!This NoodleTools workshop will use APA and/or MLA style as live demo ex
 amples\, depending on the participants that register.Don't worry! Jessica 
 will share how to use both MLA and APA. You're covered!You will learn how 
 to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to sh
 ow how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors.Al
 ong the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credible research
  in the library and on the web.Check with your instructor to confirm the c
 itation style appropriate for your research assignment.Extra Credit: As st
 udents\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course name whe
 n you register if you would like us to notify your instructor that you hav
 e attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your inst
 ructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.Regist
 ration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This workshop requires re
 gistration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.You will receive a 
 confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your sp
 am folder if you do not see it.This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes ear
 ly to allow you time to log on.Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC studen
 t conduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how 
 to join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
LAST-MODIFIED:20261113T232114Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://santarosa.libcal.com/calendar/workshops/noodletools_mla_11_24_
 26
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Join SRJC Librarian Canon Crawford to learn h
 ow to simplify citations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the w
 ay\, score quick tips on finding credible research in the library and on t
 he Web.<br />NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliog
 raphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\
 , including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.<br />Workshop 
 Details: Extra Credit available!<br />This NoodleTools workshop will use A
 PA and/or MLA style as live demo examples\, depending on the participants 
 that register.<br />Don't worry! Jessica will share how to use both MLA an
 d APA. You're covered!<br />You will learn how to sign up for an account w
 ith NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show how to create citations\
 , create a bibliography and check for errors.<br />Along the way\, you wil
 l receive quick tips on how to find credible research in the library and o
 n the web.<br />Check with your instructor to confirm the citation style a
 ppropriate for your research assignment.<br />Extra Credit: As students\, 
 you have the option to submit your instructor and course name when you reg
 ister if you would like us to notify your instructor that you have attende
 d the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on
  an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.<br />Registrat
 ion: (click "Begin Registration" button below)<br />This workshop requires
  registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.<br />You will r
 eceive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Chec
 k your spam folder if you do not see it.<br />This Zoom workshop will open
  10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.<br />Attendees are asked to
  abide by SRJC student conduct policy.<br />Not familiar with Zoom? Watch 
 this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.<br />Have questions? Ch
 at with an SRJC Librarian!
