BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/turkey-waddle-2026/", "Press Democrat": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/turkey-waddle-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/turkey-waddle-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:13th Annual Post-Thanksgiving Turkey Waddle Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T123000
UID:261029DApYaFLhJked9CFWLUX2nQ
DESCRIPTION:Jack London State Historic Park’s annual Turkey Waddle Hike 
 lets everyone get out and “shake their tail feathers” after a day of f
 easting and football.   Celebrated on the day after Thanksgiving since 2
 014\, this moderate 3.5-mile round trip hike leads through mixed evergreen
 s on the way to the majestic Ancient Redwood \\(also affectionately known 
 as the Grandmother Tree\\).\n\n Great for all ages\, “waddlers” shoul
 d wear sturdy shoes and bring water.  The trail includes uneven and rocky
  surfaces and involves some elevation gain and loss.  The event will be c
 ancelled in the event of rain. \n\n Tickets are $15 per person \\(the pa
 rk entry fee is waived\\).   Reservations and more information are avail
 able at https://jacklondonpark.com/events/turkey-waddle-2026/.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/turkey-waddle-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026greenfriday", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/family-hike-at-sugarloaf-5/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026greenfriday"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Family Hike at Sugarloaf
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T120000
UID:261012jVN04eF_ak2zmk7LwJO4nA
DESCRIPTION:Join our Docents on this fun family hike that is good for all 
 ages\, where you will learn about Sugarloaf Park\, its plants\, animals\, 
 and history. \n\nThe hike begins from the Visitor Center. One option head
 s down to the waterfall on the 2-mile Pony Gate-Canyon loop\, while a seco
 nd\, shorter option will meander along the Creekside Nature Trail. Please 
 note the route is bound to change depending on logistics such as wet cross
 ings and the participants' physical ability. Free event\, RSVP required. W
 ear layers\, appropriate footwear for slippery/rocky trails\, bring at lea
 st 32oz of water\, sun protection\, and if desired\, a snack. Parking fees
  apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026greenfriday
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T170000
UID:261004aQc8rLEbT0abCa3ADiD6Ew
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T170000
UID:260824S6rmyrZkuUme6pXEa00N1w
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\nMaple Magic & Winter Wonder invites vis
 itors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativity\
 , and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided walks\,
  hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by the c
 hanging landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the swee
 t fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experience th
 e peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
