BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://ci.ovationtix.com/35892/performance/11849295?performanceId=11849295"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Unofficial: Pardon The Interruption
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T220000
UID:261111fq-X8fM-uE6fItk_xD7wmw
DESCRIPTION:Dinner and Dancing at Rancho Nicasio with Pardon The Interrupt
 ion\n\nRoaring out of the fog-shrouded hills of Sonoma and drowning out th
 e chatter\, New Wave/Prog-Pop troubadours Pardon the Interruption \\(aka P
 TI\\) are taking their place — asserting their voice — in the storied 
 musical conversation of the San Francisco Bay Area.\n\nOne foot is planted
  firmly in the past paying homage to some of the most singular and iconic 
 artists of the ‘70s\, 80s and ‘90s. The other is stepping boldly forwa
 rd\, producing original material that is at once nostalgically familiar wh
 ile also entirely modern and unique. It’s undeniable fun. It will make y
 ou dance. It’s like a perfect pepperoni pizza. It’s Pardon The Interru
 ption.\n\nBand leader\, lead singer and guitarist David Noble \\(Wreckless
  Strangers\, Poor Man’s Whiskey\, Nina Hagen\\) has assembled three of t
 he finest\, most versatile session musicians in Northern California\, and 
 fostered a cohesion that transcends music. PTI’s love for each other and
  their craft is visceral. You can feel it.  \n\nOnline Dinner Reservation
 s from 6:00 - 8:00 pm \\(Please make a note of your reservation time\\)Mus
 ic @ 7:30Ticket price is for admission only. Dinner is NOT included in the
  ticket price.Bring your photo ID & ticket confirmation to Will Call.ALL T
 ICKET SALES ARE FINAL. No refunds or exchanges
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:https://ci.ovationtix.com/35892/performance/11849295?performanceId=118
 49295
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T220000
UID:261108e4G4xCoOLk2lB8FB3KYwvA
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\n**Trigger warnings:** Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in
  Yiddish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/rooted/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Rooted
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T220000
UID:261106oNvkbrSCY0ir5RAQ1g5-5w
DESCRIPTION:This holiday season\, Spreckels Theatre Company offers a heart
 warming alternative to traditional seasonal fare with *Rooted*\, a story a
 bout the messy\, fierce love that keeps us grounded. An intelligent\, gent
 le comedy by Deborah Zoe Laufer\, *Rooted* plays Nov. 27 – Dec.13!\n\nEm
 ery is perfectly content living in her beloved treehouse\, completely isol
 ated from the world\, communing with her plants. Meanwhile\, down on the g
 round\, her sister Hazel is thoroughly miserable\, slaving away at a dead-
 end diner job just to survive and financially support Emery’s eccentric 
 lifestyle. Looking on from the sidelines\, Luanne is yearning for somethin
 g\, anything to bring true meaning into her life.\n\n﻿The sisters' fragi
 le ecosystem is completely upended when Emery’s YouTube videos documenti
 ng her plant experiments unexpectedly go viral. Almost overnight\, her dig
 ital musings accidentally incite a full-blown CULT(!). As throngs of devot
 ed truth-seekers congregate below the treehouse\, the lives of all three w
 omen are plunged into chaos\, compelling each woman to choose their own pa
 th and find their bliss.\n\n*Pick-Your-Price Night: purchase sliding scale
  tickets starting at $10 each for the opening Friday night\, Nov. 27th.*
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts - Bette Condiotti Experi
 mental Theatre
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/rooted/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040623210?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Moonalice
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T200000
UID:261031UkidmnnDME2vRc6dbWBf5A
DESCRIPTION:Moonalice is a psychedelic\, roots-rock band of seasoned music
 ians mixing a variety of genres with extended musical improvisations that 
 evoke a sense of adventure and exploration. Everyone is a part of the expe
 rience and the music inspires dancing and other acts of self expression. E
 very show has an original art poster created by a well-known artist memori
 alizing that event and given to all attendees…each poster has its own Mo
 onalice legend. All concerts are broadcasted live in HD and available in a
 rchive shortly after their set.\n\nMoonalice plays mostly original materia
 l mixed with several covers\, and during their extended freeform jams the 
 band moves as one\, drawing from many musical genres honed from years of e
 xperience playing with various major acts. Their single "It's 4:20 Somewhe
 re" has been downloaded over 6 million times. Just released: 420 Gathering
  of the Tribe by Jay Blakesberg and Alex Fischer – a short film about th
 e Moonalice posters and poster artists: http://www.moonalice.com/song/its-
 420-somewhere. Social media: nearly 424\,000 on Facebook & over 67\,000 on
  Twitter. Their extensive tour schedule and videos of every Moonalice show
  can be seen at moonalice.com and every show poster with legends can be vi
 ewed at moonaliceposters.com.\n\nBand\n\nDylan Chambers: Vocals\, Cowbell 
 \\(Midnight Transit\, The New Chambers Brothers\\)\n\nLester Chambers: Voc
 als\, Harmonica \\(Chambers Brothers\, The New Chambers Brothers\\)\n\nJas
 on Crosby: Keyboards \\(Phil Lesh\, Terrapin Family Band\, Jenny Lewis\, J
 ohn McLaughlin\, Robert Randolph\, Blind Boys of Alabama\, Susan Tedeschi\
 \)\n\nRoger McNamee: Rhythm Guitar\, Vocals\, Bass. \\(Guff\, The Engineer
 s\, Random Axes\, Flying Other Brothers\\)\n\nJohn Molo: Drums\, Vocals. \
 \(Bruce Hornsby & The Range\, John Fogerty\, Phil Lesh & Friends\, The Oth
 er Ones\, David Nelson Band\\).\n\nPete Sears: Bass\, Keyboards\, Guitar\,
  Vocals \\(Sam Gopal Dream\, Rod Stewart\, Jefferson Starship\, Jerry Garc
 ia\, Hot Tuna\, John Lee Hooker\, David Nelson Band\, Phil Lesh & Friends\
 \).\n\nBarry Sless: Lead Guitar\, Pedal Steel Guitar\, Bass. \\(Phil Lesh 
 & Friends\, David Nelson Band\, Kingfish\, Cowboy Jazz\\).\n\nChloe Tietje
 n: Vocals \\(T Sisters\\)\n\nErika Tietjen: Vocals\, Guitar \\(T Sisters\\
 )\n\nRachel Tietjen: Vocals\, Guitar \\(T Sisters\\)\n\nFun facts\n\nMoona
 lice’s first show was in May\, 2007.\n\nMoonalice’s single\, “It’s
  4:20 Somewhere” has been downloaded more than 5 million times.\n\nMoona
 lice invented the Twittercast concert\, broadcasting links in near real ti
 me for live concerts and at random times for past shows. The band has done
  103 Twittercast concerts.\n\nMoonalice is the first band to Mooncast live
  video of all of its concerts. Moonalice has broadcast nearly ever concert
  since 2010\, the first band to operate a satellite-based broadcast system
  that enables High Definition live video to smartphones and iPads WITHOUT 
 an app!
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040623210?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108897622?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Ryan MacNeill & The Big Deal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T200000
UID:261020a2ICCPk3606diIyH2zxLog
DESCRIPTION:Experience a high-energy night of live music in Point Reyes St
 ation as Ryan MacNeill & The Big Deal take the stage at the legendary Old 
 Western Saloon.\n\nFronted by Ryan MacNeill\, whose effects-driven guitar 
 work is powered by an expansive pedalboard\, the band blends traditional s
 ongwriting with immersive textures—moving from shimmering atmospheres to
  soaring\, psychedelic-tinged leads.\n\nBacked by seasoned players deliver
 ing rich vocal harmonies\, driving basslines\, organ swells\, and dynamic 
 rhythms\, the group creates a sound that feels both grounded and otherworl
 dly.\n\nFrom late-night dives to open-road horizons\, Ryan MacNeill & The 
 Big Deal take listeners on a journey through memory\, mystery\, and the ev
 olving landscape of American music.\n\nSet in one of West Marin’s most i
 conic venues\, this promises to be an intimate\, rowdy\, and unforgettable
  night of live music.\n\nOld Western Saloon\n\n11201 CA-1\n\nPoint Reyes S
 tation\, CA 94956\n\nSaturday. November 28 2026\n\n8:00 – 11:00pm\n\n21\
 \+
LOCATION:Old Western Saloon
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108897622?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
