X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T103000
UID:2607283mKf9nvdDUKk8_wrW16nLQ
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nIn OA\, membe
 rs experience spiritual\, emotional\, and physical recovery by practicing 
 the Twelve Steps and living by their spiritual principles—one day at a t
 ime.\n\nOvereaters Anonymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who suppor
 t each other in recovering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If y
 ou feel you have a problem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what yo
 ur background\, beliefs\, or eating habits. \n\nWe hold an in-person meet
 ings at 9:30 on Sunday mornings at Church of the Nazarene\, 18980 Arnold D
 rive\, Sonoma\, CA \\(a small room directly off of parking lot\; look for 
 the sign posted\\) and newcomers are always welcome.\n\nYou may view all N
 orth Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbayoa.org/me
 etings.html\n\nOA is not a diet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembe
 rs have different plans of eating.\n\nOA does not endorse any specific foo
 d plan. \n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meeting: https:/
 /www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/the-women-of-beauty-ranch-2/", "Press Democrat": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/the-women-of-beauty-ranch-2/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/the-women-of-beauty-ranch-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Women of Jack London's Beauty Ranch: Hands That Shaped the Vis
 ion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T120000
UID:261028nJa5F4CiNkydTBV-jrY1ng
DESCRIPTION:In honor of Charmian London’s birthday on November 27\, join
  a walk celebrating her legacy and recognizing the many women whose lives\
 , work\, and creativity have helped shape the history\, culture\, and land
 scape of the park.\n\nIn the five short years Jack London lived at Beauty 
 Ranch\, he imagined it on a grand scale. That vision took root and endured
  through the labor\, intelligence\, and perseverance of two key women\, Ch
 armian Kittredge London and Eliza Shepard — who stewarded the dream\, la
 nd\, and legacy through upheaval and change\, long after Jack London was g
 one. This two-hour tour of Beauty Ranch and the House of Happy Walls Museu
 m invites visitors to step into their stories and discover how a vision be
 came an enduring reality.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/the-women-of-beauty-ranch-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
