X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/laurie-lewis-and-the-right-hands", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/laurie-lewis-and-the-right-hands/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/laurie-lewis-and-the-right-hands"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Laurie Lewis and the Right Hands
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T173000
UID:6a907e9d1fab5577542c53a7@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Bluegrass and American Roots Music\nDon't miss this incredible
  show at OCA! Bluegrass legend Laurie Lewis and her amazing band The RIght
  Hands will give us an afternoon show that you won't soon forget. Laurie w
 ill be joined by Brandon Godman\, Hasee Ciaccio and other fine musicians f
 or this performance.\nTickets are $35\, $30 for OCA members. Doors open at
  2:30 PM. Refreshments available\, free parking. Art gallery open during i
 ntermission. ADA seating available - please contact us at\ninfo@occidental
 centerforthearts.org\nfor details.\nGet Tickets\nFor nearly four decades\,
  Laurie Lewis has gathered fans and honors for her powerful and emotive vo
 ice and her versatile\, dynamic songwriting. She is a sought-after recordi
 ng producer and an equally skilled teacher and mentor.\nAnd she is an insp
 iration and a ground-breaker – across genres\, across geography and acro
 ss gender barriers.\nLaurie has shown us how a woman can blend into any pa
 rt of the classic bluegrass singing trio\, and she showed us how a great v
 oice could move fluidly between bluegrass and other types of music. She sh
 owed us how a female fiddler could emulate the strength and grit of the ea
 rly bluegrass musicians. She has shown how a Californian can appeal to tra
 ditional bluegrass audiences\, as well as winning acclaim in the worlds of
  Americana and folk music.\nShe has shown us how to lead bands of talented
  musicians – learning from them while helping them make their best music
 . And she has shown us how to thrive in a constantly changing musical envi
 ronment – without ever sacrificing her art.\n"Her voice is a rare combin
 ation of grit and grace\, strength and delicacy. Her stories always ring t
 rue."\nLinda Ronstadt
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/laurie-lewi
 s-and-the-right-hands
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts, Creative Sonoma
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.tinyurl.com/Patron-Saints-form", "Press Democrat": "http://www.tinyurl.com/Patron-Saints-form"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.tinyurl.com/Patron-Saints-form"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Patron Saints of Influence Fall Reading + Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T180000
UID:261031SNAVOb4og0KeSe1XIUq7_w
DESCRIPTION:The next Patron Saints literary reading & open mic will pay ho
 mage to mother of science fiction Mary Shelley with featured readings by L
 auren C. Johnson\, Shawna Swetech\, and Wendy M. Thompson.\n\nAs always\, 
 you are welcome to share your own written work in 5 minutes or less during
  the open mic. All words are welcome as long as they're not hateful or AI-
 generated.\n\nAbout the featured readers:\n\nLauren C. Johnson attributes 
 her upbringing in Florida–America’s weirdest state–to her interest i
 n the ecological and surreal. She's the interviews editor for The Racket J
 ournal\, where she champions experimental literature\, and is a co-founder
  and editor of Club Chicxulub\, a speculative fiction journal and reading 
 series that amplifies emerging authors. She also co-hosts Babylon Salon\, 
 one of the longest-running reading series in the Bay Area. Her short stori
 es\, interviews\, and essays have appeared in numerous journals\, includin
 g The Rumpus and Orion Magazine online. The West Façade is her debut nove
 l. Find out more at **www.laurencjohnson.com.**\n\nShawna L. Swetech is a
  retired hospital nurse\, poet\, artist and integrative health practitione
 r. Her poetry appears in Rattle\, The Healing Muse\, Pulse\, the American 
 Journal of Nursing and other journals and anthologies. Her work ranges fro
 m the personal to the universal\, the body to the body politic\, drawing f
 rom the deep wells of human nature and the natural world. Shawna is a co-h
 ost for the monthly reading series\, Rivertown Poets. She is the author of
  a newly-released poetry collection based on her 35 year career as a regis
 tered nurse\, entitled “Standing in Their Fire.” (Kelsay Books\, 2026)
  **www.ShawnaSwetech.com**\n\nWendy M. Thompson is a poet\, writer\, and 
 scholar who hails from Oakland\, California. Her debut poetry collection B
 lack California Gold (Bucknell University Press\, 2025) maps out life in t
 he Bay Area during the 1980s and 1990s and was a finalist for the 2025 Mar
 tin Cruz Smith Award: Emerging Diverse Voices prize. She has a forthcoming
  book\, Chasing the Sun: Staging Black Life\, Belonging\, and Displacement
  in California’s Bay Area (University of Washington Press\, 2027)\, that
  looks at the cultural and performative worlds of black migrants and their
  descendants who staged mobility\, home\, and refusal during Second Great 
 Migration into the contemporary era. She is an Associate Professor of Afri
 can American Studies at San José State University.
LOCATION:Shady Oak Barrel House
URL:http://www.tinyurl.com/Patron-Saints-form
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
