SUMMARY:Vallejo Community Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T190000
UID:2611076MAyHvqP6EyIyMbJS61Yow
DESCRIPTION:The City of Vallejo\, in partnership with the Greater Vallejo 
 Recreation District \\(GVRD\\)\, invites residents\, families\, and commun
 ity partners to help shape the future of Wilson Park!\n\nThe City is pursu
 ing funding through California's Statewide Park Development Grant Program 
 \\(Proposition 4\\) to support potential renovations and improvements to W
 ilson Park.\n\nThis is an exciting opportunity to explore ways to create a
  safer\, more welcoming\, accessible\, and vibrant neighborhood park for e
 veryone to enjoy.\n\nWhat Would You Like to See at Wilson Park? Your ideas
  can help identify potential park improvements\, including:\n\nNew recreat
 ional amenities and play features\n\nSafer\, more accessible spaces for al
 l ages and abilities\n\nLandscaping\, shade\, and beautification\n\nFamily
 -friendly gathering and relaxation areas\n\nOpportunities for recreation\,
  wellness\, and neighborhood connections\n\nNo final renovation plan has b
 een selected. Community input will help guide the proposed improvements.
LOCATION:GVRD Board Room
URL:https://www.gvrd.org/wilson-park-community-outreach-meetings
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/coronacapricreek/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Reimagining the Rain in Corona/Capri Creek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T193000
UID:261113WwS1pu03R0WHfRnNqxug4g
DESCRIPTION:*Si hablas español\, habrá un intérprete en este evento. In
 dícanoslo en el último paso al inscribirte en el evento.*\n\n***What wou
 ld it look like if our neighborhoods were designed to work with and welcom
 e water instead of sending it away?***\n\nAs a part of our **Harvest the R
 ain Pilot Program**\, Daily Acts is inviting Petaluma community members wh
 o live near or are frequent visitors in the **Corona/Capri Creek** area 
 to **REIMAGINE THE RAIN** by attending an interactive\, neighborhood-based
  community input session.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**Join this Community Input Session to:**\n\n*\\-Help 
 us understand your experience with stormwater*\n\n*\\-Learn from local exp
 erts in our community*\n\n*\\-Connect with your neighbors over* ***FREE di
 nner***\n\n*\\-Provide feedback on DIY rain garden and curb cut templates*
 \n\n*\\-Enter a* ***gift card drawing*** *for local businesses like Petal
 uma Coffee & Tea\, Refill Mercantile and The Seed Bank!*\n\nDuring the ses
 sion\, we'll discuss **how we can** **work with rainwater** to build resil
 ient neighborhoods. We’ll hear from you to learn where you’ve noticed 
 water pooling in your neighborhood\, and explore whether those places are 
 creating challenges\, or if they could be the beginning of an opportunity 
 to work with water in an exciting new way! We will also gather your feedba
 ck on the rain garden and curb-cut landscape templates we’re developing.
 \n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n***lf
  you live near or frequent Corona/Capri Creek\, we want to hear from you!
 ***\n\nCome share your observations\, what you’d like to see in your nei
 ghborhood\, and any questions\, excitement or concerns you may have about 
 this pilot program. We hope to see you there!\n\n*Questions? Please email
 * ***moreinfo@dailyacts.org*** *or call* ***(707) 200-8364***
LOCATION:Petaluma Community Center (Lucchesi)
URL:https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/coronacapricreek/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
