UID:261106GIoFKConf0-4RyrggkI3cQ
DESCRIPTION:Join the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation for an in-depth works
 hop on the ecology\, identification\, life history\, and conservation of t
 he San Francisco Bay Area's 16 amphibian species.\n\nLed by amphibian expe
 rts Dave Cook and Jeff Alvarez\, this workshop is designed for professiona
 l biologists\, resource managers\, environmental consultants\, students\, 
 and others working with California wildlife. The workshop combines a full 
 day of classroom instruction with a small-group field trip to a private pr
 eserve in Sonoma County.\n\n The classroom presentation takes place Frida
 y\, December 4\, 2026\, from 8:30 am to 4:00 pm at the Laguna Environmenta
 l Center. Participants will also attend one field trip on Saturday\, Decem
 ber 5\, or Sunday\, December 6. Four identical sessions are available\, wi
 th morning and afternoon options each day.
LOCATION:Laguna Environmental Center
URL:https://2026amphibiansworkshop.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
