BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/628485/latkes-light-luncheon-a-cooking-class-with-stephanie-klassen-rosenbaum"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Latkes\, Light & Luncheon: A Cooking Class at Gold Ridge Organic F
 arms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T130000
UID:261029vX274C7tSkW84PjFerOh8w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a seasonal cooking experience celebrating the Fest
 ival of Lights that brings together the best of holiday tradition and wint
 er warmth.\n\nIn this immersive lunch-and-learn\, Stephanie Klassen Rosenb
 aum will teach you step-by-step how to achieve the perfect crispy\, golden
  potato latke paired with homemade applesauce. She will also share her sec
 rets for crafting a deeply flavorful beet borscht and demonstrate how to e
 levate simple autumn side dishes—like roasted squash—with our very own
  award-winning balsamic vinegar.\n\nAfter learning the techniques\, you’
 ll gather at a cozy communal table to feast on all the dishes prepared. We
 'll finish the afternoon on a sweet note with a slice of warm\, flaky pie 
 crafted by Red Bird Bakery\, featuring Gold Ridge Organic Farms heirloom a
 pples.\n\nWhat to Expect: A scenic ride in our apple-themed trolley from t
 he Farm Shop to the Apple Cottage • A step-by-step cooking demonstration
  inside our Apple Cottage kitchen \\(no cooking required on your part!\\) 
 • Expert tips and kitchen secrets from Stephanie Klassen Rosenbaum on cr
 afting traditional dishes using fresh\, local produce • A multi-course s
 it-down lunch featuring the day's harvest menu\, enjoyed at a communal tab
 le in our organic orchard • Seasonal refreshments\, including your choic
 e of a vibrant citrus shrub or our freshly pressed apple cider • 10% off
  all Farm Shop purchases on the day of your class\n\nStephanie Klassen Ros
 enbaum is the author of seven cookbooks\, including A Little Taste of San 
 Francisco and Honey from Flower to Table. She has taught seasonal cooking 
 at farmers markets and other venues from Brooklyn to Berkeley\, including 
 the Ferry Plaza Farmers' Market in San Francisco and the Gravenstein Apple
  Fair in Sebastopol. She has cooked at numerous artists' and writers' retr
 eats including the Headlands Center for the Arts in Sausalito\, and studie
 d organic farming at the Center for Agrocology at UC Santa Cruz.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/628485/latk
 es-light-luncheon-a-cooking-class-with-stephanie-klassen-rosenbaum
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.marincounty.org/depts/cu"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Frank Lloyd Wright Civic Center Tours
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T120000
UID:261113N--7hY2tvky7pg8XHRFMQQ
DESCRIPTION:Price: Adult $10\, Senior/Full Time Student $5 \\(Plus a $2 p 
 er ticket service Charge Online\\)\n\nTicket Info:\n\nSponsor: Marin Cente
 r\n\nLink: http://www.marincounty.org/depts/cu\n\nThe Frank Lloyd Wright-d
 esigned Marin County Civic Center is a national- and state-designated hist
 oric landmark. Ninety minute docent-led tours of the Civic Center are offe
 red every Wednesday and Friday at 10:30 am\, leaving from the second floor
  Café\, Room 233. The cost is $10 adults and $5 seniors and students. No 
 reservations are required. Groups of ten or more can arrange a private doc
 ent tour by calling the Visitor Services Office at \\(415\\) 473-3762.
LOCATION:Civic Center
URL:http://www.marincounty.org/depts/cu
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
