BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.mareislandco.com/news-events/lightnight2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Mare Island Light Night - Holiday Tree Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T190000
UID:261107J2E2od32w0WGyJNC_oIygQ
DESCRIPTION:Light Night at Mare Island Friday\, December 4 | 5-7pm | Histo
 ric Core\n\nAs dusk settles over the Strait\, Mare Island glows. Come gath
 er with neighbors for our annual Holiday Tree Lighting Celebration\, a nig
 ht of music\, sweet treats\, and community spirit.\n\nSip complimentary ho
 t chocolate\, nibble on cookies\, and join us as we light the tree. Then e
 njoy a special performance by the VOENA Children’s Choir\, whose beautif
 ul voices will carry the celebration into the evening.\n\nWarm up\, give b
 ack. Bring a new or gently used coat\, or a sleeping bag\, to donate to Va
 llejo Together. Guests 21 and older who donate a coat will receive a compl
 imentary seasonal cocktail or mocktail\, compliments of The Mare Island Co
 mpany.\n\nAbout Vallejo Together\n\nVallejo Together was established as a 
 community organization in 2010 by Founder Maria Guevara to rally community
  supporters and volunteers to meet the needs of Vallejo. In 2019\, Vallejo
  Together became a fully recognized 501\\(c\\)3 non-profit organization an
 d refined their mission and vision to focus on serving the unhoused popula
 tion in Vallejo. Vallejo Together seeks to fulfill their mission of establ
 ishing reliable systems of care through collaborative partnerships\, advoc
 acy for sustainable solutions\, and offering traveling resource center ser
 vices to people without homes in Vallejo. To become a volunteer or for mor
 e information about Vallejo Together programs\, services\, and events\, pl
 ease visit www.VallejoTogether.org\n\nAbout VOENA\n\nVOENA's mission is "U
 niting the World with Children's Voices." Representing more than 35 cultur
 es\, VOENA's young singers share a message of unity\, peace\, and connecti
 on through music. Their voices have been heard on some of the world's most
  celebrated stages\, including the White House\, Carnegie Hall\, the Londo
 n Olympic Games\, and the World Expo in Japan.
LOCATION:Mare Island Historic Core
URL:https://www.mareislandco.com/news-events/lightnight2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/merry-bright/20329741/2026-12-04T17", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/merry-bright/20329741/2026-12-04T17"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Merry & Bright
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T190000
UID:261106phR1GfWQYEO0_GfCN3wceg
DESCRIPTION:**Step into Santa Rosa’s premier winter wonderland for the 6
 th Annual *Merry & Bright*!**\n\nPresented by Sonoma Clean Power\, produce
 d by the Redwood Ice Theatre Company (RITC)\, and hosted at iconic Snoopy
 ’s Home Ice\, this cherished holiday tradition returns with nine complet
 ely free outdoor ice skating shows. Gather the family to watch dazzling ro
 utines from professional skaters\, accompanied by classic holiday music an
 d seasonal entertainment designed to bring neighbors together across Sonom
 a and Mendocino counties.\n\nIn the spirit of innovation and sustainabilit
 y\, this year’s outdoor production is powered directly by Sonoma Clean P
 ower’s all-electric Ford F-150 Lightning truck—showcasing clean energy
  in action while helping local households discover easy ways to save energ
 y this winter.\n\n**Admission:** Completely free\, no tickets required!\n\
 n**Location:** Snoopy’s Home Ice\, Santa Rosa\n\n**Show Schedule (9 Free
  Outdoor Performances):**\n\n**Friday\, December 4:** 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p.m
 .\n\n**Saturday\, December 5:** 2:00 p.m.\, 3:00 p.m.\, 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p
 .m.\n\n**Sunday\, December 6:** 1:00 p.m.\, 2:00 p.m. & 3:00 p.m.\n\n**Pro
  Tip:** Arrive early to bundle up\, grab a hot cocoa\, and secure the best
  spot to watch the show!\n\nTo learn more about how SCP is giving back thi
 s holiday season\, visit: https://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
LOCATION:Snoopy's Home Ice
URL:https://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109080973?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Matt Jaffe
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261204T170000
UID:261031I2fWkTZHnkC-2ui-M_sLUw
DESCRIPTION:Matt Jaffe is an indie rock & roll singer/songwriter from San 
 Francisco. Cutting his teeth on countless open mics around the Bay\, Matt 
 started taking music \\(a little bit\\) more seriously when Jerry Harrison
  of Talking Heads offered to produce his first record. Since then\, Matt h
 as continued to churn out more songs than he can remember the words to\, p
 erform on stages throughout the land \\(opening and/or touring with the li
 kes of Mavis Staples\, Wilco\, Bob Weir\, Jackie Greene\, Chuck Prophet\, 
 Melissa Etheridge\, and Blues Traveler\\)\, and collaborate with Tom Higge
 nson of the Plain White T's. Inspired by the likes of Elvis Costello\, Tom
  Petty and Stephin Merritt\, Matt is continuously writing and recording to
  build a songbook that honors his heroes.  Along with serving on Bread & R
 oses Board of Directors\, he is currently rolling out his 7th studio album
 \, Gone Enough to Miss.
LOCATION:MacRostie Winery Estate House
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109080973?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
