DESCRIPTION:Our very own Petaluma Women’s Chorus presents the shimmering
  sounds of snowy nights and winter twilight in their “Winter’s Night
 ” concert at 4 pm on Sunday\, December 6\, in downtown Petaluma. The con
 cert features Leo Delibes’ lovely Messe Breve and the spirited “Boa No
 ite\, Minha Gente\,” a festive Brazilian song for women inspired by the 
 “baiana” celebration. This is the Chorus’ first season singing in ou
 r new home\, the historic Hall of the Above at 199 N. Petaluma Blvd. (the 
 corner of East Washington and Petaluma Boulevard). We can’t wait for you
  to hear the sound of the full choir performing in the great acoustics of 
 this beautiful space! See you there. Tickets are available via Square Paym
 ent system (link included here) or at the door. Tickets $20 General Admiss
 ion $15 Students Sadie Sonntag\, Artistic Director Lori Sikorski\, Accompa
 nist
