DESCRIPTION:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliogr
 aphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\,
  including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details
 : Extra Credit available!You will learn how to sign up for an account with
  NoodleTools. We will also provide examples to show how to create citation
 s\, create a bibliography and check for errors. There will be time to ask 
 questions at the end of the overview —bring your sources along. Join us 
 for a workshop and learn how to cite your sources right!Extra Credit: As s
 tudents\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course name wh
 en you register if you would like us to notify your instructor that you ha
 ve attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your ins
 tructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.Regis
 tration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This workshop does not r
 equire registration. However\, registering will guarantee admittance to th
 is in-person workshop. Please arrive promptly.Workshop Location: Santa Ros
 a Campus\, Doyle Library\, Room 4327. See map for directions to Doyle Libr
 ary.The workshop will open 5 minutes prior to the start time.Attendees are
  asked to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.Have questions? Chat with a
 n SRJC Librarian!
