BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.mccunecollection.org"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Nov & Dec Artwalks: "Moments in the Light"  Plein Air Painting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T210000
UID:261110LDVAXg4GI06pOjovk7RkPw
DESCRIPTION:Plein Air painting is painting on location responding to the e
 nvironment as it moves you. For us it’s not about the details or exact c
 haracteristics of a location but rather the interaction of color\, the atm
 osphere\, the feeling of standing out there. It's about the immediate mome
 nt of seeing which is in the brushwork of several of the artists\, creatin
 g a dialogue with the space as you make the marks and see how they corresp
 ond to what's in front of you. There is no right or wrong because it is a 
 very personal moment. It's not impressionism. It's not quite expressionism
 . But it's the immediacy of being alive. \n\nMost of the paintings were d
 one when Barry convinced one of the other artists to come painting with hi
 m. Creating a synergy from the overlapping influence on each other while k
 eeping a distinct POV.
LOCATION:McCune Collection
URL:http://www.mccunecollection.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/lantern-walks/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/lantern-walks/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/lantern-walks/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Winter Wonder Lantern Walks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T183000
UID:261023VVoKfXlbvUW1n0fKnHFqBA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the beauty and quiet magic of the season during Wint
 er Wonder Lantern Walks\, a festive after-dark experience at Sonoma Botani
 cal Garden. Guided along the route by Garden staff and volunteers\, guests
  will stroll through the winter landscape carrying glowing lanterns\, disc
 overing softly shadowed pathways\, towering trees\, and the peaceful still
 ness of the Garden beneath the night sky. Rather than a traditional docent
 -led tour\, this experience is designed as a peaceful and immersive opport
 unity to enjoy the rare experience of walking through the Garden after hou
 rs and after dark. Along the way\, enjoy moments of reflection\, seasonal 
 ambiance\, and the simple joy of gathering outdoors during the holiday sea
 son.\n\nThe evening begins with hot cocoa\, spiced cider\, wine tasting an
 d cookies from 5:30–6:00 p.m.\, followed by a brief welcome and lantern 
 walk orientation before departing together for a guided walk through the G
 arden.\n\nWinter Wonder Lantern Walks are a seasonal fundraiser that will 
 support the Garden’s programs\, collections\, and conservation efforts. 
 PLEASE READ the important accessibility and experience information\, along
  with the registration and cancellation policy below before purchasing tic
 kets.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/lantern-walks/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://vallejoartwalk.org"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Vallejo 2nd Friday Artwalk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T210000
UID:261111TDoSmp6VskybZtz5_nnOfQ
DESCRIPTION:A free monthly community arts event! Since 2014\, Artwalk ener
 gizes downtown Vallejo every 2nd Friday of the month from 5 to 9 pm.\n\nVa
 llejo has a vibrant arts community. You'll find local artists\, hand made 
 crafts\, gallery openings hosted by local artists\, open shops\, restauran
 ts\, live music\, and so much more! Outdoor vendors set up on the 600 bloc
 k of Marin Street\, between Georgia and Virginia Streets and additional ve
 ndors\, activities\, and arts and culture happenings are all throughout th
 e entire downtown area. Join our email newsletter at vallejoartwalk.org to
  learn more details about the event. Come out and enjoy! There is always s
 omething new!
LOCATION:Downtown Vallejo
URL:http://vallejoartwalk.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Bright Nights at Cuvaison
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T190000
UID:261110PM0zCfyLBEuqnXvaSLYt9Q
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the magic of the holiday season with Bright Nights\,
  an evening wine tasting experience set against one of Cuvaison’s most e
 nchanting backdrops: rows and rows of estate vineyards illuminated with tw
 inkling lights.\n\nOffered Friday\, Saturday\, and Sunday evenings from No
 vember 27 through January 3\, Bright Nights invites you to experience the 
 beauty of wine country after dark as the vineyard comes alive with a warm 
 holiday glow. From 5:00pm to 7:00pm\, settle in for a cozy seasonal tastin
 g featuring a selection of Cuvaison wines served with seasonal cheese and 
 charcuterie pairing.\n\nWhether you’re gathering with friends\, celebrat
 ing the season\, or creating a new holiday tradition\, Bright Nights offer
 s a festive and memorable way to enjoy the estate.\n\nExperience Highlight
 s:\n\n·         Rows of estate vineyards illuminated with twinkli
 ng holiday lights\n\n·         Curated wine and cheese pairings\n
 \n·         Festive evening tasting from 5:00pm to 7:00pm\n\n· 
         A magical seasonal setting for friends and holiday gatherin
 gs\n\nThis special tasting experience is offered Fridays\, Saturdays and S
 undays from November 27 through January 3\, with reservations beginning at
  5:00\, 5:15\, and 5:30pm. Please include all guests in your reservation.\
 n\nCuvaison and Brandlin Estate members receive preferred pricing and will
  see a $35 discount for up to 4 guests applied at checkout. Please use the
  email address where you receive membership updates in order for your disc
 ount to apply.\n\nCuvaison kindly asks that all guests be 21 years of age 
 or older to enjoy this experience (unless otherwise noted for special fami
 ly friendly dates). The patio is closed during Bright Nights\, so Cuvaison
  is not able to accommodate pets.\n\nImportant Dates:\n\nThursday\, Novemb
 er 12 – Industry Event\n\nSaturday\, November 15 – Member Pick-up Even
 t + Holiday Shopping\n\nFriday\, November 27 – Bright Nights Launch + Bl
 ack Friday Specials\n\nThursday\, December 3 – Bright Nights Workshop ev
 ent\n\nSunday\, December 13 – Bright Nights Family Night (includes milk 
 + cookie pairing for kids\, and a holiday activity). This evening may also
  include a photographer offering Holiday Family portraits.\n\nSunday\, Dec
 ember 27 – Bright Nights Family Night (includes milk + cookie pairing fo
 r kids\, and a holiday activity). This evening may also include a photogra
 pher offering Holiday Family portraits.
LOCATION:Cuvaison Estate Tasting Room
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://newmooncircus.ticketspice.com/new-moon-circus", "Press Democrat": "https://newmooncircus.ticketspice.com/new-moon-circus"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://newmooncircus.ticketspice.com/new-moon-circus"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:New Moon Circus Presents ‘La Lune Brille
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T183000
UID:261023g0W7xdtneEWLLz2fewCa7g
DESCRIPTION:New Moon Circus Presents ‘La Lune Brille’: a highly origin
 al\, all-human circus that enchants through breathtaking acrobatics and at
 hletically stunning skill.\n\nSonoma\, CA— November 27 - Dec 27 – This
  2026 winter season\, New Moon Circus invites audiences to ‘La Lune Bril
 le’ — memorable family fun and stunning artistry under the intimate an
 d charming atmosphere of the ‘petite’ big top.\n\nMeet the Winter moon
  and her frenemy\, the Sun.  When the moon is pushed from the sky\, she m
 ust find a way home to the stars. Come along the journey as she encounters
  mysterious beings and friendly creatures on the way.\n\nA child pleasing 
 origin myth told through impressive aerialists\, jugglers\, acrobats\, and
  clever comedy\, this show blends classic storybook atmosphere with celest
 ial magic. La Lune Brille will surprise\, dazzle and delight all ages.\n\n
 Spectators for all showings are invited to the European style circus tent 
 to experience the magic up to 30 minutes before each show. Cornerstone Son
 oma will provide light concession and libations for purchase. \n\nThe eve
 nt will include a 15 minute intermission during the 1 and a half hour show
 .\n\nLimited free parking is available at the location at Cornerstone Sono
 ma.\n\nTickets for La Lune Brille are now available for purchase online at
  thenewmooncircus.com.\n\nIndividual ticket prices start at $40. Front row
  \\(VIP\\)\, options start at $65. Find showtimes and more details at then
 ewmooncircus.com. Early booking is encouraged for this highly anticipated 
 event.
LOCATION:CORNERSTONE SONOMA - Under the Big Top Tent
URL:https://newmooncircus.ticketspice.com/new-moon-circus
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
