BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/belonging-to-ourselves-understanding-attachment-trauma-and-building-resilience-with-mindfulness-and-in-community-pb1d26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/belonging-to-ourselves-understanding-attachment-trauma-and-building-resilience-with-mindfulness-and-in-community-pb1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/belonging-to-ourselves-understanding-attachment-trauma-and-building-resilience-with-mindfulness-and-in-community-pb1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Belonging to Ourselves: Understanding Trauma & Building Resilience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T160000
UID:261012sqNuewVDJ06ifevMpr7Y8Q
DESCRIPTION:with Pawan Bareja\, PhD and Diane Poole Heller\n\nWe begin lif
 e with a child’s open heart\, full of trust\, innocence\, and pure joy. 
 Yet\, over time\, the world leaves its marks. We often arrive at our medit
 ation cushions carrying a lifetime of hidden grief\, from the lingering ac
 he of a breakup to the quiet sorrow of a loveless childhood. To protect ou
 rselves from this attachment trauma\, we build walls that close us off fro
 m the very people we wish to love.\n\nThis daylong is an invitation to ret
 urn home to the pure love that is your true nature. We do not heal in isol
 ation\; we heal together. Our nervous systems are beautifully social\, wir
 ed to find safety\, warmth\, and co-regulation in the presence of others.\
 n\nIf accepting love feels foreign\, you can break those protective patter
 ns. Through guided meditations\, gentle reflection\, and supportive group 
 connections\, we will mend broken bonds\, navigate love and conflict\, and
  rebuild our lasting resilience.\n\nDiane will lead a practical teaching s
 ession drawing on her background in nervous-system-informed approaches to 
 attachment\, offering an embodied complement to the day’s content.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/belonging-to-ourselves
 -understanding-attachment-trauma-and-building-resilience-with-mindfulness-
 and-in-community-pb1d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.gvrd.org/wilson-park-community-outreach-meetings"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Wilson Park Community Outreach Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T113000
UID:261107_sUQRsCHG0Wx2tU7w73myA
DESCRIPTION:The City of Vallejo\, in partnership with the Greater Vallejo 
 Recreation District \\(GVRD\\)\, invites residents\, families\, and commun
 ity partners to help shape the future of Wilson Park!\n\nThe City is pursu
 ing funding through California's Statewide Park Development Grant Program 
 \\(Proposition 4\\) to support potential renovations and improvements to W
 ilson Park.\n\nThis is an exciting opportunity to explore ways to create a
  safer\, more welcoming\, accessible\, and vibrant neighborhood park for e
 veryone to enjoy.\n\nWhat Would You Like to See at Wilson Park? Your ideas
  can help identify potential park improvements\, including:\n\nNew recreat
 ional amenities and play features\n\nSafer\, more accessible spaces for al
 l ages and abilities\n\nLandscaping\, shade\, and beautification\n\nFamily
 -friendly gathering and relaxation areas\n\nOpportunities for recreation\,
  wellness\, and neighborhood connections\n\nNo final renovation plan has b
 een selected. Community input will help guide the proposed improvements.
LOCATION:GVRD Board Room
URL:https://www.gvrd.org/wilson-park-community-outreach-meetings
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T170000
UID:261004V-0MOIQg_USd5lfvUj8T9Q
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
