X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T170000
UID:260430qY4_l96N00SMDhYxgROnbQ
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.fvaa-arts.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:FSVAA 63rd Annual Nor-Cal Regional Juried Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T180000
UID:261113MU_CsUSUw0mJCcrBYbiQlA
DESCRIPTION:2026 Juried Art Exhibit: Celebrating Northern California’s A
 rtistic Excellence!\n\nFSVAA proudly presents the 63rd Annual Nor-Cal Regi
 onal Juried Art Show at the Solano Town Center Gallery – show opening is
  Friday\, Nov 13. Gallery Hours are Wed thru Sun\, 11am–6pm.\n\n The th
 ree jurors\, Ferdinanda Florence\, Nadja Fitchhorn\, and Vickie Marchand h
 ave spoken and made their selections!\n\nWe received 200 art entries from 
 67 talented artists representing 15 different cities throughout Northern C
 alifornia\, making this an exciting and impressive year for our Juried Art
  Show.\n\nIt was wonderful to see so many artists arrive with their treasu
 red works of art\, eager to have them reviewed and considered by our three
  distinguished jurors.\n\nAfter careful deliberation\, the jurors selected
  97 outstanding works of art to be included in this year's Juried Art Show
 !\n\nCongratulations to all the artists whose work was selected\, and than
 k you to everyone who participated and helped make this year's show such a
  success.\n\nEXHIBIT INFORMATION \\(Save the Dates\\):\n\n• Art Show Rec
 eption /Awards Gala: Saturday\, Dec 5\, 2026\, 3–5pm\n\n• Reception /P
 oetry Reading: Saturday\, Dec 19\, 2026\, 3–5pm\n\n• Juror's Talk: Sun
 day\, Jan 3\, 2027\, 1–3pm at the Solano Town Center Gallery  – Come 
 hear our Jurors speak! Join us as they share their insights into the selec
 tion process\, discuss what goes into choosing artwork for a juried exhibi
 tion\, and offer a glimpse into their experience. As always\, there will b
 e time for a Q&A\, so bring your questions!
LOCATION:Solano Town Center Gallery
URL:https://www.fvaa-arts.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
