SUMMARY:Stuffed and Decorated Vessels with Vicki Assegued (December 13th\,
  2026) — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261213T000000
DTEND:20261214T000000
UID:b8cbe487c93560e84e39ec55ac77ff92@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Stuffed and Decorated Vessels with Vicki Assegued (December 13
 th\, 2026)\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $125.00\n        \n   
    \n    \n  \n\nRegister early to qualify for our $25.00 off early-bird r
 egistration rate!Use code VCK-EARLYBIRD-1213 until November 13th to claim 
 your discountStuffed and Decorated VesselsInstructor: Vicki Assegued Where
 : Sebastopol Center for the Arts When: Sunday\, December 13th\, 2026- 10:0
 0am-3:00pmPrice: $100 registration + $25 Materials Fee Class Description: 
 You’ll create a free-form multi-fabric textile\, then turn it into a ves
 sel shape\, stuff it\, and add a vast array of wonderful fiber and decorat
 ive elements to make a super unique and fun piece of art. No art experienc
 e is necessary\, and all levels are most welcome. This class is perfect fo
 r beginning through experienced students. Please bring: Sewing needle and 
 thread\, Fabric Scissors (If you have them)Optional: You’re encouraged t
 o bring materials from your own stash including fabrics\, used clothing\, 
 yarn\, string\, lace\, ribbon\, beads\, old jewelry parts and other decora
 tions.Another upcoming class with this instructor: Saturday Jan 30\, 2027 
 - Fibers Beyond the FrameAbout the Instructor: Vicki Assegued is an experi
 mental and innovative fiber artist and instructor\, always finding new and
  unique ways to work with textiles and fibers. Through her creative proces
 s\, she explores many ways to weave\, layer\, attach\, coil\, tie\, knot\,
  twist\, build and develop her pieces so they are vibrant and engaging. Sh
 e then shares all of her techniques with her students\, supporting and ins
 piring them to fully engage in their own creative process of discovery and
  expression. Vicki teaches at art schools and retreats around the country\
 , such as the Art & Soul Mixed Media Retreat\, the Mendocino Art Center\, 
 North Country Studio Workshops and the San Jose Museum of Quilts & Textile
 s. Vicki completed a 4-month residency with the Santa Cruz Recycled Art Pr
 ogram. She has exhibited and sold her work at galleries\, businesses\, hea
 lth centers\, restaurants\, community centers\, museums\, and open studio 
 events. You can learn more about Vicki here: https://www.vickiart.com/\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n
