BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_c_rilc5rtgatnr4oln08fo9p5k30
SUMMARY:Focus Night: Geminids Meteor Shower
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T210000
DTSTAMP:20261114T061708Z
UID:05qsjqdscqbs8jc9d7eb517sms@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T190000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20261016T070817Z
DESCRIPTION:Move over\, summer Perseids. December's Geminid shower is cons
 idered the best and most reliable meteor shower of the year. Under dark cl
 ear skies\, counts can reach 50-100 per hour or more on peak night. But th
 is is only one of many factors that set these meteors apart from all other
  showers. Their speed and composition create meteors that flare low in the
  atmosphere\, are easier to spot\, and leave bright\, often yellow\, trail
 s. <br><br>This is one of the very few showers visible all night long. Wh
 at causes this dazzling display and why does it occur at this time of year
 ? Come learn about these unique meteors\, their unusual history\, and thei
 r mysterious origin. <br><br>This Focus Night equips you for a Geminid 
 ”peak” experience. Unlike planets that can hang around for months\, a 
 meteor shower is only visible over a short period of time. Highest counts 
 will occur later in the night and into the early morning hours. You will l
 earn about different kinds of showers\, how best to view them\, and how to
  understand what you are seeing. You’ll also discover factors that influ
 ence meteor counts and how to optimize your viewing. <br><br>Plan to be i
 n the classroom by 6:55PM to ensure you have a good seat. Program begins p
 romptly at 7:00PM . Sales are limited to 40 guests so we can provide a mor
 e personal experience. Allow generous time to arrive and park. <br><br>Pl
 ease visit <a href="https://rfo.simpletix.com/" target="_blank">https://r
 fo.simpletix.com</a> for important information and to buy tickets. You MU
 ST have a ticket to attend this event\; tickets will not be sold at the do
 or. Cost includes the Sugarloaf Ridge State Park parking fee. Please note 
 that tickets are non-refundable and cannot be used for future events.<br><
 br>RFO is operated by the Valley of the Moon Observatory Association\, a 5
 01(3)(c) nonprofit organization. All proceeds go toward maintaining this b
 eloved Sonoma County institution.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261016T070817Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Robert Ferguson Observatory
END:VEVENT
