X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:Young\, Gifted\, and Black - Art Submissions Due
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
DTSTAMP:20261008T101910Z
UID:20261218T080000Z-24102@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20261218
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,941,941/744_cs_-_young_gifted_black_art_submission.r
 ev.1791479937.png
CATEGORIES:Museum
DESCRIPTION:Young\, Gifted\, and Black: Art by Black Students at SRJC is a
 n upcoming exhibition at the SRJC Multicultural Museum celebrating the cre
 ativity and artistic voices of Black students across campus. Created in re
 cognition of Black History Month\, the exhibition provides a dedicated spa
 ce for Black student artists to have their work seen\, valued\, and celebr
 ated by the SRJC community.  Black students are invited to submit original
  artwork in any medium or theme\, including visual art\, poetry\, and othe
 r forms of creative writing. Artwork does not need to focus on Black ident
 ity or the Black experience—the exhibition celebrates the breadth of Bla
 ck creativity and the individuality of each participating artist.  The exh
 ibition will be on display in the ground floor library display cases from 
 the beginning of the Spring 2027 semester through Spring Break. Students i
 nterested in participating must drop off their work at the SRJC Multicultu
 ral Museum by December 18\, 2026.Learn more about the museum on the SRJC M
 ulticultural Museum website. (https://museum.santarosa.edu/)
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T171910Z
LOCATION:Multicultural Museum - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/24102-young-gifted-and-black-art-
 submissions-due
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Young\, Gifted\, and Black: Art by Bla
 ck Students at SRJC</em> is an upcoming exhibition at the SRJC Multicultur
 al Museum celebrating the creativity and artistic voices of Black students
  across campus. Created in recognition of Black History Month\, the exhibi
 tion provides a dedicated space for Black student artists to have their wo
 rk seen\, valued\, and celebrated by the SRJC community.</p><p>  Black stu
 dents are invited to submit original artwork in any medium or theme\, incl
 uding visual art\, poetry\, and other forms of creative writing. Artwork d
 oes not need to focus on Black identity or the Black experiencethe exhibit
 ion celebrates the breadth of Black creativity and the individuality of ea
 ch participating artist.</p><p>  The exhibition will be on display in the 
 ground floor library display cases from the beginning of the Spring 2027 s
 emester through Spring Break. Students interested in participating must dr
 op off their work at the SRJC Multicultural Museum by December 18\, 2026.<
 /p><p><a href="https://museum.santarosa.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopene
 r">Learn more about the museum on the SRJC Multicultural Museum website.</
 a></p>
