BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_c_rilc5rtgatnr4oln08fo9p5k30
SUMMARY:Deep Sky Astrophotography Processing class (class 2 of 3)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270211T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270211T203000
DTSTAMP:20261114T061708Z
UID:591p6modr3bpfeg8lal40724te@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270211T183000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260827T171716Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Have you ever admired amazing deep sky astrophotography ima
 ges and wondered if you could ever create similar images?  Now you can! 
   </p><p>With raw data provided from the telescopes at the Robert Fergus
 on Observatory\, in this class series of three sessions you will have the 
 opportunity to learn how to process and edit your own beautiful deep sky i
 mages. <strong>Please note\, this workshop is meant as a 3-class series. 
 It is highly recommended to purchase tickets for all three days.</strong><
 /p><p><strong>Please note\, this is a virtual class. A Zoom link will be s
 ent to participants prior to the class.</strong> </p><p>What you will lea
 rn in this class:</p><p>- The fundamentals of Deep Sky Astrophotography</p
 ><p>- An overview of image capture techniques (a dedicated\, hands-on clas
 s on Deep sky image capture using your own equipment will be held later in
  Spring 2025)</p><p>- Robert Ferguson Observatory Image capture techniques
  - how we captured the data that will be used in this class.</p><p>- An ov
 erview of image processing techniques</p><p>- An introduction to Siril\, a
  free and open-source Astronomical Image Processing Program</p><p>- A hand
 s-on session where you will process data collected at the Robert Ferguson 
 Observatory </p><p>- A wrap-up session where you will have the opportunit
 y to share and discuss your images with other class attendees</p><p> </p>
 <p>Class Prerequisites:</p><p>- A computer newer than 5-years old (the new
 er the better)\, loaded with the latest operating system</p><p>- At least 
 8MB of RAM (more is better)</p><p>- At least 50GB of free disk space (pref
 erably a solid-state disk drive.  More storage is better)</p><p>- Famili
 arity with creating directories\, moving files between folders\, setting f
 older and file permissions\, and accessing cloud drives.</p><p><br></p><p>
 Get more information and purchase tickets at <a href="https://www.google.c
 om/url?q=http://rfo.simpletix.com&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=
 1788200536774383&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3o4TzEdWTplI6Unc8Ziywm" target="_blank">rf
 o.simpletix.com</a>.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260827T171716Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:Robert Ferguson Observatory
END:VEVENT
